          "end_line":750,
          "quote": "Only\n`satisfied` establishes the predicate. `falsified` establishes that the\npredicate fails and names the counterexample. `indeterminate`,\n`out_of_frame` and `invalid_basis` establish neither, and each names what\nwould decide: the evidence, the missing relation or capability with its\nowner where the subject gives one, or the basis repair. By support for the\npredicate, `satisfied` stands above each other value, and the other four\nare not ordered among themselves.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults",
          "start_line":743
        },
        {
          "end_line":762,
          "quote": "- an evaluation that was not performed stays distinct from one whose\n  evidence cannot decide: it has no\n  [closed result](ACTIVATION.md#7-closed-result-and-reuse), and it is never mapped\n  to `indeterminate` or to any other core value;\n- an effect whose completion is unknown never maps to no effect or to\n  completed.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults",
          "start_line":757
        }
      ],
      "key": "result_recording_and_standing",
      "statement": "Every performed evaluation returns one core value or exactly mapped refinement and records its evaluated predicate, core value and original domain outcome. Domain meaning remains with the defining member/profile/Product; consumers needing its distinctions read the domain outcome. Result standing concerns the predicate and differs from commitment standing: only satisfied establishes it, falsified establishes failure with its counterexample, and the other three establish neither and identify deciding evidence, missing relation/capability and its given owner, or basis repair. No mapping or refinement raises standing: failed/falsified or undecidable outcomes cannot become success; non-performance maps to no core value; unknown effect completion cannot become no effect or completion. Actors cannot report evaluations they did not perform. Failed, indeterminate, out-of-frame, out-of-scope and invalid-basis outcomes keep their declared outcomes rather than being coerced to satisfied.",
      "uncertainty": "Specific domain mappings, including out-of-scope outcomes, require their defining owners."
    },
